title ALES139 — Lotus's stereo_halve: the half-wave rectifier carried into stereo, one shared threshold at zero, the EVEN+ODD member of the even corner
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Second lap of this recur turn (after ALES138 stereo_rectify opened the even corner and sent). The ALES138 log named the half-wave (ALES85) and inverted half-wave (ALES86) as the next agent-doable cruxes to complete the even family. Taking the half-wave is the crux-first continuation — a proven pattern with a genuinely distinct story, not a mechanical repeat.
think ALES85 lives in halve.rye: halve(clip, start, count), y = max(x, 0), keep the positive half and silence the negative. HalveError = {BadRange} only — no gain, no ceiling, and crucially NO rail edge (max(x,0) is exact for every i16, a negative simply becomes 0), so no saturate is owed. Even plainer than the full-wave lift. Validated the span once against the shared length, ran mono halve per channel, reused HalveError whole.
think The fresh story: where the full-wave rectifier (ALES138) COLLAPSED an out-of-phase master to identical channels, the half-wave PARTITIONS it. Keeping only the positive half means at each index exactly one of {left, right} survives — a sample and its negation cannot both be positive. Proved two facts at every index: left[i]·right[i] = 0 (disjoint, never both sounding) and left[i] + right[i] = |left[i]| (the two half-waves summing to the full-wave magnitude — max(x,0) + max(-x,0) = |x|). Also proved a 1:2 master keeps its ratio on the kept samples, idempotence, non-negativity on both, the span discipline, and BadRange atomicity. Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean.
think Self-caught tidy: an early draft of the partition test carried a stray no-op line (a dead if-with-empty-block); removed it before building so the selftest reads clean. The final proof asserts the disjointness product and the partition sum directly against the original magnitudes.
obs The even corner now holds two of its three readings — the full-wave collapse (ALES138) and the half-wave partition (ALES139). The image lesson keeps widening honestly: linear/copy maps PRESERVE the image, not-odd maps BREAK the antisymmetry, the even full-wave COLLAPSES it to mono, and the even+odd half-wave PARTITIONS it into disjoint one-sided channels. The inverted half-wave (ALES86, halve_neg.rye, y = min(x,0)) is the natural next lap — it keeps the negative half, the mirror of this rung, and with it the rectifier family stands whole in stereo (max(x,0) + min(x,0) = x). No custody gate reached: purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round.
loom witness=ales_stereo_halve_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=nonlinear axis=even-odd cases=image-partitioned+disjoint+sum-is-magnitude+ratio-held+idempotence
file lotus/stereo_halve.rye ALES139 — stereo_halve, the half-wave rectifier lifted to stereo: one shared threshold at zero on both channels, validated once (span only, no saturate owed), four laws with the image-partition law (an out-of-phase master returns two disjoint one-sided channels summing to the full-wave magnitude, the honest contrast with the image-collapsing full-wave) and idempotence.
file tools/ales_stereo_halve_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-halve line.
file active-designing/20260815-040747_fill-ales139-lotus-stereo-half-wave-rectifier.md the self-approved design read for this rung.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES139 roster entry on the Status line, stamp refreshed.
recommend keep-going the inverted half-wave (ALES86, y = min(x,0)) lifts into stereo next by the same proven pattern, completing the rectifier family in stereo (max(x,0) + min(x,0) = x); a plain agent-doable crux with no gate reached. Purely local; the increment sends as its own signed round.
